1. Definitions

"Software" means the original project code and documentation offered under
this license, including modifications. "Licensor" means a copyright holder
offering their contribution under this license. "You" means a recipient
exercising the granted rights.
"Commercial Use" means use primarily intended for or directed toward
commercial advantage or monetary compensation, including sale, paid access,
paid hosting or services, advertising-supported or sponsored monetization,
use to operate or promote a business, or incorporation in a commercial
product or service. Nonprofit status alone does not make use noncommercial.
"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for modifying the Software,
including all original and modified source code, scripts needed to build,
install and run it, dependency manifests, and configuration templates. It
excludes real credentials, private user data, general-purpose tools, and
unmodified third-party dependencies available separately.

