Statutory exceptions and limitations remain intact.

3. Attribution

Retain copyright notices, this license, third-party rights notices, and the
original project URL in every source distribution. Credit "WitchCat
contributors", link to the original project, and identify material changes
and their dates. Binary distributions must include the same information in
accompanying documentation or an accessible legal/about page. A deployed web
interface must retain a reasonably visible "Powered by WitchCat" credit
linking to the original project in its footer or an equivalent about page.
Credit must not suggest endorsement by a Licensor.

4. Source disclosure and same license

When distributing the Software or a modified version in any form, provide its
complete Corresponding Source under this exact license. Binary distributions
must include an easily discoverable link to a public repository or source
archive corresponding to that exact version. Access must be free of charge,
without login or other access restrictions.

When deploying the Software, including a modified version, for others to
interact with over a network, prominently offer those users the same free
public access to the complete Corresponding Source of the deployed version.
Link the source offer from the interface or an accessible about page; for an
API-only service, include it in service documentation.

Keep source available while distributing or operating that version and for
at least three years after the last distribution or operation. Private
modifications neither distributed nor deployed for others do not trigger
publication. Publishing source does not authorize Commercial Use. Do not
relicense the Software or Your modifications, impose additional restrictions,
or use technical measures preventing recipients exercising these rights.
Independent works merely aggregated with the Software retain their licenses.

5. Third-party works and trademarks

Third-party libraries, runtimes, fonts, images, music, models and other assets
are excluded unless their copyright holder explicitly offers them under this
